  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday morning through next Saturday)\nIssued at 200 PM EDT Sun Oct 18 2026\n\nOverall benign weather will continue through much of this week. Our \narea will be stuck between the slowly meandering vertically stacked \nlow pressure system off the east coast and ridging to our west. Sfc \nhigh pressure is expected to prevail through the next 7 days as a \nresult with a dry airmass expected to continue. PWATs at or below \n0.5\" are forecast as a result with near 0 rain chances. Plenty of \nsunshine and clear skies along with subsidence will allow for day \ntime highs to creep into the mid to upper 70s through the week but \novernight lows will continue to be in the low to mid 40s across the \nregion. The only concern will be fire weather conditions. With dry \nair in place there are chances for increased fire danger each day \nthrough next week.",
